Source: material-grub
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: LucaCraft89 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/LucaCraft89/material-grub
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: material-grub
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, material-boot-core (>= 1.0.0), grub-common, librsvg2-bin, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-pil
Description: Material 3 Expressive GRUB theme, built from source on your machine
 The package contains the sources only. The theme is rendered when the package is
 installed or updated, with the same safety nets as the installer: the new
 grub.cfg is validated, rolled back if it is not valid, and the failure is
 reported without failing the package transaction.

Package: material-grub-gui
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, material-grub (= ${source:Version}), python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pil, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: librsvg2-bin
Description: Optional graphical editor for the Material GRUB theme
 A local web UI (it opens in your browser) to switch styles, recolour, rename,
 reorder and hide boot entries, edit Ventoy sticks, save presets and update,
 with a live preview. It never runs as root itself: changes go through polkit.
 Not installed with the theme.
